            <ArticleTitle>Familial hypophosphatemia: an unusual presentation with low back ache, heel pain, and a limp in a young man, and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>585-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10067-010-1607-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of young man with low back ache and heel pains who was examined in a rheumatology outpatient and diagnosed as familial hypophosphatemia (FH), probably X-linked (XL), is presented. FH is most commonly transmitted as XL. The role of PHEX gene and fibroblast growth factor 23 is also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
